## Section 3: Outgoings and housing costs

Do this last. It needs income answers (childcare eligibility) and `property_owned`.

### CCQ behaviour

`Steps::OutgoingsSection` (only when income questions are not skipped):

```
outgoings
[partner_outgoings]       only if partner
property [property_landlord]   (see Property)
housing costs step:
  shared_ownership_housing_costs   if property_owned == "shared_ownership"
  mortgage_or_loan_payment         if property_owned == "with_mortgage"
  housing_costs                    unless owns outright
  (nothing)                        if owns outright
```

`none` (and unanswered) falls into `housing_costs`.

| Step | CCQ form | Session keys | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `outgoings` | `OutgoingsForm` | per `childcare_payments`, `maintenance_payments`, `legal_aid_payments`: `_relevant`, `_conditional_value`, `_value`, `_frequency` | Childcare question only appears when `ChildcareEligibilityService` is true: client has child dependants, and (student finance, or any non-`statutory_pay` income), and the same for the partner. Value `> 0` when relevant. Frequencies: `every_week`, `every_two_weeks`, `every_four_weeks`, `monthly`, `total` (`total` removed for controlled) |
| `partner_outgoings` | `PartnerOutgoingsForm < OutgoingsForm` | same, `partner_` prefix | Same behaviour. Same childcare rule |
| `housing_costs` | `HousingCostsForm` | `housing_benefit_{relevant,value,frequency}`, `housing_payments`, `housing_payments_frequency` | Payments `>= 0`. Frequency required when payments `> 0`. Housing benefit value `> 0` when relevant, and must not exceed annual housing costs |
| `mortgage_or_loan_payment` | `MortgageOrLoanPaymentForm` | `housing_loan_payments`, `housing_payments_loan_frequency` | Payment `>= 0`. Frequency required when `> 0` |
| `shared_ownership_housing_costs` | `SharedOwnershipHousingCostsForm` | `housing_benefit_*`, `shared_ownership_mortgage`, `rent`, `combined_frequency` | `rent` and mortgage `>= 0`. Frequency required when the combined amount `> 0`. Housing benefit must not exceed combined annual costs |

Special case: for shared ownership in the change-answers loop, CCQ sends the user back through `property_entry` (`display_property_entry_in_change_answers?`). This is already in `navigation.ts`. Check that the check-your-answers change flow uses it.

### Today

Every step is one free-text field with a made-up code (`housing_costs`, `mortgage_or_loan_payment`, `shared_ownership_housing_costs`, `partner_outgoings`). `outgoings` has the right field codes for all three payment types, but its frequency values are `weekly` / `fortnightly` / `four_weekly` / `monthly` / `three_monthly`, not CCQ's. The childcare question is always shown, and nothing checks eligibility or the `_value` attribute.

